Z||000000||BAM-BAM||04-03-2000||08:14 AM||||     I was wonderingif ahyone knows of an alternate automatic trans for the Fiero. Is there any swaps that can be made fairly simpley? any advise is appriciated.<P>  Thanx, BAN-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfixit58||04-03-2000||10:00 AM||||I was doing a little research in this area a few weeks back. Unfortunatly, I didn't get too far. Someone gave me this link:<BR> <A HREF="http://hometown.aol.com/kit440t4/myhomepage/business.html" TARGET=_blank>http://hometown.aol.com/kit440t4/myhomepage/business.html</A> <P>I've sent a few notes to the Email address on the page but have not received a response as of yet. His site makes mention of new axles needed but I can't confirm.<P>I've also thought about the newer transmission that is used behind the 3800 (4L60T??? or something like that). This transmission will handle a lot more torque and, since I'm planning on at least a 3.4 conversion, I'm leaning toward this transmission. I know ACE's site( <A HREF="http://www.americancustomeng.com/)" TARGET=_blank>http://www.americancustomeng.com/)</A>  mentions a transmission conversion kit but I can find a price or discription on the site. It'll probably require an Email or phone call.<P>I probably wasn't much help but at least we're on the same page. If you find any of the above info, I'd appreciate it if you could post it or send me a copy directly.<P>See Ya,<BR>Roy ||||reg||1
Z||000002||phillip||04-03-2000||10:33 AM||||got a couple of old kit car mags that i picked up for their fiero swap artictles(7-'98 and 4-'87). says it's possible and works well. dosen't go to much into difficulty of the swap. it dose say the newer electronicly controled trannys are about 100 lbs. heavier. says no adaptation cost auto to auto. articles are both only a couple of pages long so i guess it gives possibillities and you find out the specifics.<P><BR>sources they list: <BR>gary zumalt<P>joe wynmam associated auto, inc.<P>chris west <P>john noman car parts depot<P>fiero doc, fiero motorsports<P>fiero phil, focoa<P>pisa<P>IRM<P>ACE<P>design one systems<P>v8 archie<P>both mags are a few years old but the sources may still be good. i know some are. hope this helps. ||||reg||1
